  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{\u2032}(t)=\u27e8-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(t)\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(t)\\,,3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3t)\u27e9\n$$\n\n and $F(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\u27e84,\\,-2\u27e9.$\n\n$F(t)=\u27e8${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \u27e8-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(t)\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(t)\\,,3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3t)\u27e9\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \u27e8-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(t)\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(t)\\,,3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3t)\u27e9\\text{d}t & =\u27e8\\int -\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(t)\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3t)\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(t)+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3t)+{c}_{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\u27e84,\\,-2\u27e9$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\u27e8\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e84,\\,-2\u27e9 \\\\ \u27e81+{c}_{1},\\,-1+{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e84,\\,-2\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=3$ and ${c}_{2}=-1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=\u27e8\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(t)+3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3t)-1\u27e9.\n$$",
